LOCUS       Yash_Matched_5P         4328 bp    DNA              SYN 12-NOV-2026
DEFINITION  Yash matched-normal design known DNA segment before unspecified
            PolyA; partial construct.
ACCESSION   YASH_MATCHED_5P
VERSION     YASH_MATCHED_5P
KEYWORDS    .
SOURCE      synthetic construct
  ORGANISM  synthetic construct
            artificial sequences.
COMMENT     Local design identifier, not an assigned INSDC accession.
            Unspecified. Reference feature matches do not establish that the
            supplied DNA context is a complete circular plasmid.
            Generated by this design's run.py and genbank.py. Pinned annotation
            evidence: annotation-sources.json; selected antigen records:
            selected_regions in annotation-sources.json. Stable region_id and
            event_id values are preserved in standard /note qualifiers.
            RNA Foundry backbone sequence source: supplied PL3092 example. Cap
            chemistry and nucleotide modifications are unspecified. Feature
            coordinates describe the designed sequence, not measured cleavage or
            antigen presentation.
            PARTIAL CONSTRUCT: only the known upstream sequence is exported.
            PolyA length and format, any downstream extension and the template
            boundary depend on the final architecture and are unspecified. No
            complete RNA/template sequence or total length is assigned.
